cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Equivariant monad bundles on CICY free quotients — a
  defect-audited scan
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata
  below. Prefer the concept DOI, which always resolves to
  the latest version.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Franck
    family-names: Sachet
    orcid: 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22095895'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/francksachet/cy-landscape-monads'
abstract: >-
  A systematic scan of two-term monad bundles over complete
  intersection Calabi-Yau threefolds admitting a free
  quotient, aimed at three-generation heterotic models. The
  scan covers 194 CICYs with |chi| = 3|Gamma|, 14943
  candidate identities and 505601 verdict lines, computed in
  a single state of the code. Two candidates are fully
  verified, both SO(10) with Z2, three generations; both are
  semi-positive and therefore lie outside the 7118 positive
  monads of arXiv:0911.1569. A limitation of principle
  closes the line: a Wilson line preserves the rank of the
  gauge group, SO(10) has rank 5 and the Standard Model rank
  4. All verdicts are computed mod p with the reserve stated
  explicitly, and the work has had no independent
  verification. Nine implementation defects found during the
  work, none of them by the code itself, are documented
  together with the discipline that caught them.
keywords:
  - heterotic string
  - Calabi-Yau
  - monad bundles
  - complete intersection Calabi-Yau
  - free quotients
  - Wilson lines
  - string phenomenology
  - computational reproducibility
